    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d980">

                <pb facs="1035" n="1023" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg1023"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 European War 1939/2025½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-30">December 30, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary agrees that it is inopportune to pursue further at this time the
                    question of the adoption by Russia of proposals to agree <pb facs="1036"
                        n="1024" xml:id="pg1024"/> to the Geneva Convention. We have urged directly
                    upon the Russian Government our opinion in the matter and we have presented it
                    to the Russian Government through the intermediation of its ambassador [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">minister</hi>] to Stockholm. Under those circumstances
                    we have done what we could and it is now felt that we should refrain from any
                    particular urging upon the Russian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>B[<hi rendition="#small-caps">reckinridge</hi>] L[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ong</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
